Z||000026||stimpy||09-27-2001||10:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 007DOUG:<BR><B><BR>Come on. I smell something.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think it's called  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>I know what would make this story more believeable to me... TWIN TURBOS!<BR>Everytime Mr. 85 gt posts on this subject, it becomes more and more laughable. "Another company" shuffles off a mint 88 GT to "dads friend's yard" because he "doesn't mess with Fiero's". I mean, the car "turned over with a jump" and "few clicks of the key". How much "messing with Fieros" would that shop have to have done? I don't care if it's a Wartburg or a Lada, ifit's in "mint" shape, it's going for FAR more then $50.<BR>Besides, what shop is going to drop everything they are doing to try to get a $50 car started for a 16 year old kid who doesn't even have the $50 in his pocket? I can walk into a shop with $500 and practically have to sleep with someone to get helped.<P>Sorry bro. There are a lot of truly gullible folks on this forum. But I ain't the one.<BR>||||reg||1
